{%- comment -%}
  Montibello PDP — EDITORIAL: benefits / features.

  Visual card version of `montibello.features`. Renders the product-specific
  benefit section from the official PDP structure (e.g. HOP Ultra Repair
  Shampoo's "El primer paso en tu rutina de cuidado") — `feature.title` is
  the benefit-section heading, `feature.description` the bullet body. No new
  product-level metafield was created for the heading; the feature
  metaobject's own `title` field serves that role (Phase 4F decision).

  Renders whenever any referenced feature has a title or description — an
  icon/image is optional and purely decorative when present, never required
  to show the section (HOP's product-specific features currently have no
  image, since no exact authoritative icon asset exists per product).

  `montibello.features` is a list of `montibello_feature` metaobject
  references — accessed with direct dot notation (`feature.title.value`),
  not `feature.fields.title.value`.

  `feature.description` is Rich text (`rich_text_field`), rendered with
  `| metafield_tag` on the field drop itself below — `.value` is used only
  for the blank/presence check, never for HTML output.

  LUXLIGHT LAYOUT (Supreme Lightener 9+ visual-parity reset): a live
  screenshot audit of https://hair.montibello.com/producto/supreme-lightener-9/
  found the official "Máxima aclaración..." block is NOT a centered card
  grid — it's a left-aligned heading followed by single-line benefit
  statements separated by divider rules (already stored as separate
  paragraph nodes in `feature.description` — one `<p>` per line via
  `metafield_tag`, so no data reshaping was needed, only CSS). There is also
  no generic "Beneficios" label on the official page; the feature's own
  title IS the heading. Both are range-gated to `range == 'LUXLIGHT'` so
  HOP's already-verified centered card grid is untouched.

  PHOTO LAYOUT (manager-feedback closure pass, HOP Ultra Repair Shampoo —
  "DIAGRAMAR CORRECTAMENTE CON IMAGEN A LA IZQUIERDA"): when a non-Luxlight
  feature now has `feature.image` populated (an official editorial photo,
  not a small icon), it renders as a real 2-column image-left/text-right
  row instead of the centered icon-grid card, matching the official
  structure. Values match the same measured system already used on the
  range pages (sections/montibello-hop-luxlight-media-frame.liquid,
  montibello-under-layout.liquid): 650:462 media ratio, 12px radius,
  rgb(246,246,243) background, 40px/35px heading scale — kept consistent
  site-wide rather than inventing new numbers for this one section.

  MULTI-SECTION LUXLIGHT PDPs (Luxlight 8-PDP official parity pass): the
  official pages for Supreme Control Oil Lightening System 2+ and Supreme
  pH Protective Shampoo / Supreme Acidic pH Treatment each have TWO
  distinct lower editorial sections (not one) — confirmed via a live DOM
  audit of hair.montibello.com (see scripts/scratch/luxlight-8-audit.json
  used during that pass). The layout below is decided PER FEATURE, not
  once for the whole section/product: any feature with an image renders
  its own full-width photo row (each is its own `<div>`, not a shared grid
  cell), stacked with real vertical spacing between rows — this is what
  makes "N features with images" render as N independent official-style
  sections instead of forcing a 2-up icon grid. A feature with no image
  still falls back to the original centered icon-grid card, unchanged.

  ORIENTATION MAPPING (LUXLIGHT FINAL VISUAL FIX pass — supersedes the
  prior "both rows image-right" rule): that prior pass applied the
  manager's screenshots literally, which made BOTH editorial rows on
  Control Oil/pH Shampoo/Acidic Treatment text-left/image-right — visually
  flat, not a zig-zag. This pass's brief is explicit: the FIRST editorial
  block on each of these 3 products must be IMAGE-LEFT/TEXT-RIGHT, and the
  SECOND must be TEXT-LEFT/IMAGE-RIGHT (the official zig-zag rhythm),
  confirmed per-product:
    - Control Oil: [0] "Una herramienta versátil..." (benefits) = image
      left; [1] "Múltiples servicios" (results) = image right.
    - pH Shampoo: [0] "Reparador y protector del pH" (benefits) = image
      left; [1] "Tratamiento luxlight que eleva los resultados"
      (ph-results-shared) = image right.
    - Acidic Treatment: [0] "Hidratación y reparación profunda..."
      (benefits) = image left; [1] same shared "ph-results-shared"
      feature = image right.

  Kept the same explicit feature-HANDLE map (`image_right_feature_
  handles`) — not a `product.handle` conditional; this keys off the
  stable `montibello_feature` metaobject handle, the same identifier
  already used everywhere else in this file to look products/features up.
  Only each product's SECOND ("results"/shared) feature handle is listed
  now; each product's FIRST ("benefits") feature handle was removed from
  the list so it falls through to the default (image-left), producing the
  zig-zag. Lightener 9+ and Clay-7+'s single photo-row features remain
  NOT in this list, unchanged (image-left, already correct). Adding a
  future Luxlight product's feature handle here is the full extent of
  what's needed to onboard it; this is the "safe feature-id/title mapping"
  tier, not a chain of `if product.handle == ...` branches.

  Still adding a real `image_position` field to the metaobject definition
  remains blocked: this app's OAuth client isn't granted
  `write_metaobject_definitions` (only write_files/write_metaobjects/
  write_products — confirmed via a live scope check). If that scope is
  ever granted, this map should be replaced by reading the field directly.

  BOLD LEAD-IN PHRASES (Part 7): "Múltiples servicios" and "Tratamiento
  luxlight que eleva los resultados" both render an inline `<strong>` lead
  phrase before each line on the official page (e.g. "Base breaker: aclara
  suavemente..."). The underlying `description` rich text for exactly these
  two metaobjects was corrected this pass (via the same script) to carry a
  real `bold: true` text node for the lead phrase — `| metafield_tag`
  already renders that as `<strong>`, so no markup logic was needed here,
  only the data fix.

  STRETCHED MEDIA HEIGHT (Parts 8–9): the official photo rows show the
  image spanning close to the full height of its text column, not a
  shorter fixed-aspect-ratio crop floating beside a taller text block
  (measured live: e.g. Control Oil's "Una herramienta versátil" section is
  430px tall, its image 380px — image-to-text height parity, not a small
  image in a tall section). Switched the photo-row grid to
  `align-items: stretch` with the image at `height: 100%; object-fit: cover`
  instead of a fixed `aspect-ratio`, so the image genuinely stretches to
  match whichever column (text or image) ends up taller — the old fixed
  650:462 ratio is kept ONLY as a mobile-width fallback where there is no
  second column to stretch against.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% liquid
  assign range = product.metafields.montibello.range.value
  assign features = product.metafields.montibello.features.value
  assign has_feature_content = false
  for feature in features
    if feature.title.value != blank or feature.description.value != blank
      assign has_feature_content = true
    endif
  endfor

  assign is_luxlight_layout = false
  if range == 'LUXLIGHT'
    assign is_luxlight_layout = true
  endif

  # UNDER FINAL 20/20 MICRO-POLISH: the official UNDER editorial result rows
  # are separated by clear divider lines (confirmed live on all 4 official
  # pages) — this photo-row previously had NO row dividers at all for
  # UNDER (plain stacked paragraphs), unlike Luxlight's own divider variant.
  # Reuses the exact same visual treatment as `--luxlight` under its own
  # modifier class, scoped so Luxlight/HOP are untouched.
  assign is_under_layout = false
  if range == 'UNDER'
    assign is_under_layout = true
  endif

  # HOP ULTRA REPAIR — TRUE OFFICIAL PARITY FINAL: the official editorial
  # "girl" block separates its result lines with a thin, PALE divider line
  # (confirmed live — NOT black/bold like UNDER's own divider requirement)
  # — Peru's default (non-Luxlight/non-Under) photo-row style has no
  # divider at all between these lines. Reuses the shared pale
  # `var(--color-border, #e4dfd4)` already used everywhere else on this
  # theme as the default hairline, not a new color. Scoped to the 4 real
  # Ultra Repair products via the `subfamily` metafield — HOP's other
  # subfamilies (Colour Last/Keratin) are untouched.
  assign hop_subfamily = product.metafields.montibello.subfamily.value
  assign is_hop_ultra_repair_layout = false
  if range == 'HOP' and hop_subfamily == 'Ultra Repair' or range == 'HOP' and hop_subfamily == 'Color Last' or range == 'HOP' and hop_subfamily == 'Smooth Hydration'
    assign is_hop_ultra_repair_layout = true
  endif
  # FULL-SITE PARITY: UNDER / Luxlight products that carry their official
  # gallery use the same official PDP system as the HOP families (full-bleed
  # beige editorial band, 630/630 grid, 0.5px #767676 rules).
  assign benefits_official_gallery = product.metafields.montibello.official_gallery.value
  if benefits_official_gallery != blank
    if range == 'UNDER'
      assign is_hop_ultra_repair_layout = true
    elsif range == 'LUXLIGHT'
      assign is_hop_ultra_repair_layout = true
    endif
  endif

  # UNDER — Carta de Color CTA relocation (final punctual fix): the official
  # Permanent Colour page shows the black "CARTA DE COLOR" button INSIDE the
  # lifestyle photo-row itself — right column, directly under the 4 result
  # lines, part of the same copy block. It was previously its own section
  # (montibello-shade-browser) rendered well below with its own background,
  # which read as a separate detached band no matter how much its top
  # padding was reduced. Moved the CTA markup into THIS row's copy instead.
  # Gated on `has_shades` (not just `is_under_layout`) because the activator
  # products share this same section/template instance but have no shades
  # metafield data — this keeps the CTA on Permanent Colour only, with zero
  # per-product `product.handle` branching.
  assign shades_primary = product.metafields.montibello.shades.value
  assign shades_overflow = product.metafields.montibello.shades_overflow.value
  assign has_shades = false
  for shade in shades_primary
    assign has_shades = true
    break
  endfor
  unless has_shades
    for shade in shades_overflow
      assign has_shades = true
      break
    endfor
  endunless
  assign show_shade_cta = false
  if is_under_layout and has_shades and section.settings.shade_chart_url != blank
    assign show_shade_cta = true
  endif

  assign has_icon_only_feature = false
  for feature in features
    if feature.image.value == blank
      assign has_icon_only_feature = true
    endif
  endfor

  # Explicit feature-handle → image-right map (see ORIENTATION MAPPING doc
  # comment above). Comma-delimited with leading/trailing commas so the
  # `contains` check below can't false-positive on a handle that happens to
  # be a substring of another.
  assign image_right_feature_handles = ',feature-luxlight-supreme-control-oil-lightening-system-results,feature-luxlight-supreme-ph-results-shared,'
%}

{% if has_feature_content %}
  <div
    class="section section--{{ section.settings.section_width }} montibello-pdp-benefits{% if is_luxlight_layout %} montibello-pdp-benefits--luxlight{% endif %}{% if is_hop_ultra_repair_layout %} montibello-pdp-benefits--hop-ultra-repair{% endif %} spacing-style"
    style="{% render 'spacing-style', settings: section.settings %}"
  >
    {% comment %}
      All icon-only (no-image) features share ONE compact centered grid with
      ONE heading, exactly as before this pass — rendered first, once, not
      per-feature (a per-feature heading would repeat it for every card).
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {% if has_icon_only_feature %}
      {% if is_luxlight_layout == false and section.settings.heading != blank %}
        <h2 class="montibello-pdp-benefits__heading">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
      {% endif %}
      <div class="montibello-pdp-benefits__grid">
        {% for feature in features %}
          {% if feature.image.value == blank %}
            <div class="montibello-pdp-benefits__card">
              <div class="montibello-pdp-benefits__copy">
                {% if feature.title.value != blank %}
                  <h3 class="montibello-pdp-benefits__title">{{ feature.title.value }}</h3>
                {% endif %}
                {% if feature.description.value != blank %}
                  <div class="montibello-pdp-benefits__description">{{ feature.description | metafield_tag }}</div>
                {% endif %}
              </div>
            </div>
          {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    {% endif %}

    {% comment %}
      Every feature WITH an image gets its own full-width image-left/text-
      right row, stacked in order — N features with images render as N real
      stacked official-style sections (e.g. Supreme Control Oil Lightening
      System 2+ and Supreme pH Protective Shampoo / Supreme Acidic pH
      Treatment each have two on the official page), not a forced grid.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {% assign photo_row_n = 0 %}
    {% for feature in features %}
      {% if feature.image.value != blank %}
        {% assign photo_row_n = photo_row_n | plus: 1 %}
        {% comment %}
          Explicit handle map decides orientation — see the ORIENTATION
          MAPPING doc comment above. Default (handle not listed) is
          image-left, matching Lightener 9+/Clay-7+'s untouched behavior.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {% assign feature_needle = feature.system.handle | prepend: ',' | append: ',' %}
        {% assign is_image_right = false %}
        {% if image_right_feature_handles contains feature_needle %}
          {% assign is_image_right = true %}
        {% endif %}
        <div
          class="montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row{% if is_luxlight_layout %} montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row--luxlight{% endif %}{% if is_under_layout %} montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row--under{% endif %}{% if is_hop_ultra_repair_layout %} montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row--hop-ultra-repair{% endif %}{% if is_image_right %} montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row--image-right{% endif %}"
          {% if is_luxlight_layout %}data-montibello-reveal{% endif %}
        >
          <div class="montibello-pdp-benefits__grid">
            <div class="montibello-pdp-benefits__card">
              <div class="montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-wrap">
                {{
                  feature.image.value
                  | image_url: width: 800
                  | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', class: 'montibello-pdp-benefits__icon', widths: '400,600,800'
                }}
              </div>
              <div class="montibello-pdp-benefits__copy">
                {% if feature.title.value != blank %}
                  <h3 class="montibello-pdp-benefits__title">{{ feature.title.value }}</h3>
                {% endif %}
                {% if photo_row_n > 1 and is_luxlight_layout %}
                  {%- comment -%} official mobile: the second editorial block collapses behind a "Ver resultados" row {%- endcomment -%}
                  <input type="checkbox" id="{{ section.id }}-benefit-toggle-{{ photo_row_n }}" class="montibello-pdp-benefits__toggle-input">
                  <label class="montibello-pdp-benefits__toggle-label" for="{{ section.id }}-benefit-toggle-{{ photo_row_n }}">Ver resultados <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></label>
                {% endif %}
                {% if feature.description.value != blank %}
                  <div class="montibello-pdp-benefits__description">{{ feature.description | metafield_tag }}</div>
                {% endif %}
                {% if show_shade_cta and forloop.last %}
                  <a
                    class="montibello-pdp-benefits__shade-cta"
                    href="{{ section.settings.shade_chart_url }}"
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener"
                  >
                    <span class="montibello-pdp-benefits__shade-cta-icon" aria-hidden="true">
                      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18">
                        <path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 01-2 2H5a2 2 0 01-2-2v-4m4-5l5 5 5-5m-5 5V3"></path>
                      </svg>
                    </span>
                    {{ section.settings.shade_chart_label | default: 'Descargar Carta de Color' }}
                  </a>
                {% endif %}
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
{% endif %}

{% stylesheet %}
  .montibello-pdp-benefits__toggle-input,
  .montibello-pdp-benefits__toggle-label {
    display: none;
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    /* official mobile result rows: ~35px pitch with a light hairline */
    .montibello-pdp-benefits .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row--luxlight .montibello-pdp-benefits__description p,
    .montibello-pdp-benefits .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row--under .montibello-pdp-benefits__description p {
      padding: 7px 0;
      border-bottom: 0.5px solid #767676;
    }

    .montibello-pdp-benefits__toggle-label {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      padding: 15px 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid #cfcfcf;
      font-size: 23px;
      line-height: 21px;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: -0.02em;
      cursor: pointer;
    }

    .montibello-pdp-benefits__toggle-input:not(:checked) ~ .montibello-pdp-benefits__description {
      display: none;
    }
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits__heading {
    max-width: 1400px;
    margin: 0 auto 24px;
    padding-inline: 20px;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 26px;
    font-weight: 700;

    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      padding-inline: 30px;
    }
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 32px;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 1400px;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: 20px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    /* min(180px, 100%) — see montibello-product-ingredients.liquid for why
       a bare fixed-px minmax floor overflows narrow viewports. */
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(180px, 100%), 1fr));
    text-align: center;

    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      padding-inline: 30px;
    }
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits__card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits__copy {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits__icon {
    display: block;
    width: 56px;
    height: 56px;
    object-fit: contain;
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits__title {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits__description {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    opacity: 0.8;
  }

  /* LUXLIGHT: left-aligned heading + divider-separated single-line rows,
     matching the official "Máxima aclaración..." block — not a centered
     card grid. `feature.description` already renders one <p> per line via
     `metafield_tag`, so only the paragraph spacing/border needs styling. */
  .montibello-pdp-benefits--luxlight .montibello-pdp-benefits__grid {
    display: block;
    max-width: 700px;
    margin-inline: 0;
    padding-inline: 20px;

    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      padding-inline: 30px;
    }
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits--luxlight .montibello-pdp-benefits__card {
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 0;
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits--luxlight .montibello-pdp-benefits__title {
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    font-size: 24px;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-align: left;

    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      font-size: 28px;
    }
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits--luxlight .montibello-pdp-benefits__description {
    width: 100%;
    text-align: left;
    opacity: 1;
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits--luxlight .montibello-pdp-benefits__description p {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 14px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border, #e4dfd4);
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits--luxlight .montibello-pdp-benefits__description p:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  /* PHOTO ROW: image left / text right, matching the official structure and
     reusing this site's established range-page media system (measured
     against hair.montibello.com — see sections/montibello-hop-luxlight-
     media-frame.liquid and montibello-under-layout.liquid for the original
     measurements): 650:462 ratio, 12px radius, rgb(246,246,243) background,
     40px/35px heading scale, 1300px contained width, 48px column gap.

     ONE ROW PER FEATURE WITH AN IMAGE (Luxlight 8-PDP parity pass): some
     official products have two of these stacked editorial sections in a
     row (e.g. Supreme Control Oil Lightening System 2+, Supreme pH
     Protective Shampoo, Supreme Acidic pH Treatment) — each `.photo-row` is
     its own independent block so N features with images render as N real
     stacked sections, with real vertical spacing between them, not a
     forced 2-up card grid. */
  .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row {
    background-color: rgb(246, 246, 243);
    padding-block: 40px;
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row + .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row {
    margin-top: 4px; /* hairline separation so two stacked rows still read as distinct sections */
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row .montibello-pdp-benefits__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 24px;
    max-width: 1300px;
    text-align: left;

    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      column-gap: 48px;
      /* STRETCH, not center: the image should span the same height as the
         text column (measured live — see the STRETCHED MEDIA HEIGHT doc
         comment above), not float vertically centered at a shorter fixed
         crop next to a taller text block. */
      align-items: stretch;
    }
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row .montibello-pdp-benefits__card {
    display: contents;
  }

  /* IMAGE-RIGHT variant (Part 6/9 — alternating rhythm, then the explicit
     handle map in the FINAL 20/20 pass): swaps the two grid children's
     visual order without touching source order, so the DOM/reading order
     (heading → copy, then image) stays sane for screen readers regardless
     of which side the image renders on.

     NOTE #1: `.grid > .icon` (direct-child combinator) would NOT match —
     `.card` has `display: contents`, which changes the rendered BOX tree
     (so its children visually behave like direct grid children) but does
     NOT change the actual DOM tree the `>` combinator matches against.
     Fixed (an earlier pass) to a descendant selector.

     NOTE #2 (FINAL 20/20 pass — found live, same class of bug): after the
     image/text-height-parity fix wrapped the `<img>` in `.photo-wrap` and
     made the `<img>` itself `position: absolute` (so it stops contributing
     to grid track sizing — see the STRETCHED MEDIA HEIGHT doc comment),
     `.icon` ALSO stopped being a grid item at all — `.photo-wrap` is now
     the actual grid item. `order` on `.icon` therefore did nothing
     (confirmed live: `--image-right` class present, but image still
     rendered at x:70 instead of the right column). Selector corrected to
     target `.photo-wrap`, the element that's actually a grid item now. */
  .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row--image-right .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-wrap {
    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      order: 2;
    }
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row--image-right .montibello-pdp-benefits__copy {
    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      order: 1;
    }
  }

  /* PHOTO WRAP (final micro-polish pass — ROOT CAUSE FIX): the previous
     `height: 100%` directly on the <img> did NOT make the image match the
     text column's height — it made the ROW match the IMAGE's own natural
     aspect ratio instead, then stretched the (short) text column down to
     fill that. Measured live on Lightener 9+: the source photo is a tall
     1440×2016 portrait crop, so at its rendered column width the image's
     intrinsic height was 834px — the grid's auto row-track sizing counted
     that intrinsic height as this row's max-content contribution, so the
     text column got stretched to match 834px too (visible as a short block
     of copy floating in a much taller column — exactly the "image feels
     longer than the text" complaint). A percentage height on a normal
     in-flow image still contributes its OWN intrinsic size to grid track
     sizing regardless of the stretch intent.

     Fix: `.photo-wrap` is the actual grid item (contributes ~0 intrinsic
     height, no in-flow content of its own) and is stretched to the row's
     auto height — which is now driven ONLY by `.copy`'s real content
     height, exactly the "image runs from where text begins to where it
     ends" target. The `<img>` inside is taken out of flow (`position:
     absolute; inset: 0`) so it never contributes to sizing, and is cropped
     via `object-fit: cover` to fill whatever height `.copy` established. */
  .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-wrap {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
    aspect-ratio: 650 / 462;

    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      height: 100%;
      aspect-ratio: auto;
      /* Floor/ceiling so a very short text column (e.g. a 2-line feature)
         still gets a real, elegant photo rather than a sliver, and a very
         long one doesn't blow the image back up to portrait-scale. */
      min-height: 320px;
      max-height: 560px;
    }
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row .montibello-pdp-benefits__icon {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: 12px;

    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      position: absolute;
      inset: 0;
    }
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row .montibello-pdp-benefits__copy {
    text-align: left;
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row .montibello-pdp-benefits__title {
    font-size: 35px;
    font-weight: 700;

    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      font-size: 40px;
    }
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row .montibello-pdp-benefits__description {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    opacity: 0.85;
  }

  /* LUXLIGHT PHOTO ROW: same image-left/text-right 2-column shape as above,
     but keeps Luxlight's own divider-row text treatment (left-aligned
     heading + one <p> per line with a border under each) instead of the
     default's paragraph style. Confirmed against the live official Supreme
     Lightener 9+ page before building — "FALTA IMAGEN Y EL TEXTO VA AL
     LADO DERECHO". `!important` on background-color: some other equal/
     higher-specificity rule elsewhere was overriding a plain declaration
     here to transparent (root cause not fully identified) — kept, matching
     the established pragmatic-fix pattern used elsewhere in this codebase. */
  .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row--luxlight {
    background-color: rgb(246, 246, 243) !important;
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row--luxlight .montibello-pdp-benefits__title {
    text-align: left;
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row--luxlight .montibello-pdp-benefits__description {
    opacity: 1;
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row--luxlight .montibello-pdp-benefits__description p {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 14px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border, #e4dfd4);
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row--luxlight .montibello-pdp-benefits__description p:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  /* UNDER PHOTO ROW (FINAL 20/20 MICRO-POLISH): same divider-row text
     treatment as Luxlight's own variant above (left-aligned heading + one
     <p> per result line with a border under each) — UNDER's editorial rows
     previously had NO dividers at all (plain stacked paragraphs), while
     the official UNDER pages show a clear line under every row. Uses a
     visibly dark/black divider (not the pale `#e4dfd4` beige used
     elsewhere) per this pass's explicit "black divider line" requirement —
     confirmed against the official page's own visibly dark row rules.
     Scoped to its own `--under` modifier class so Luxlight/HOP are
     untouched. */
  .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row--under .montibello-pdp-benefits__description {
    opacity: 1;
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row--under .montibello-pdp-benefits__description p {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 14px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(17, 17, 17, 0.85);
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row--under .montibello-pdp-benefits__description p:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  /* HOP ULTRA REPAIR — forensic official layout (measured 1440 on
     hair.montibello.com/producto/ultra-repair-shampoo): full-bleed
     rgb(246,246,243) band that is CONTIGUOUS with the hero band above it
     (25px block padding on both), 630px photo (900:640, 12px radius) +
     40px gap + 630px copy column, heading 40/40 wrapping inside 470px,
     result rows 16/19.7 with 20px below + 0.5px #767676 rule + 20px gap —
     every row (the last included) carries its rule. Scoped to the modifier
     so every other range/subfamily is untouched. */
  .montibello-pdp-benefits--hop-ultra-repair {
    font-family: 'TTCommons', 'Montserrat', sans-serif;
    background-color: #f6f6f3 !important;
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 100vmax #f6f6f3;
    clip-path: inset(0 -100vmax);
    padding-block: 25px !important;
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits--hop-ultra-repair * {
    font-family: inherit;
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row--hop-ultra-repair {
    padding-block: 0;
    background-color: transparent !important;
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row--hop-ultra-repair .montibello-pdp-benefits__grid {
    max-width: 1300px;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: 20px;

    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      /* fluid columns capped at the official 630px: 20px page margin and gap
         below 960px, 30px margin from 960px, 40px gap from 1200px, flush
         1300px container from 1360px (fixed 630+630 overflowed the window) */
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 630px));
      column-gap: 20px;
      padding-inline: 20px;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
    }

    @media screen and (min-width: 960px) {
      padding-inline: 30px;
    }

    @media screen and (min-width: 1200px) {
      column-gap: 40px;
    }

    @media screen and (min-width: 1360px) {
      padding-inline: 0;
    }
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row--hop-ultra-repair .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-wrap {
    aspect-ratio: 900 / 640;
    border-radius: 12px;

    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      height: auto;
      min-height: 0;
      max-height: none;
      aspect-ratio: 900 / 640;
    }
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row--hop-ultra-repair .montibello-pdp-benefits__copy {
    gap: 0;
  }

  /* two stacked editorial rows (official: two 498px sections, 25px above/below
     each image row and 50px under the last) */
  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row--hop-ultra-repair + .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row--hop-ultra-repair {
      margin-top: 21px;
      margin-bottom: 25px;
    }
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .montibello-pdp-benefits--hop-ultra-repair {
      padding-inline: 0 !important;
      padding-block: 25px !important;
    }

    .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row--hop-ultra-repair .montibello-pdp-benefits__grid {
      padding-inline: 0;
      gap: 20px;
    }

    .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row--hop-ultra-repair .montibello-pdp-benefits__title {
      max-width: none;
      font-size: 35px;
      line-height: 35px;
    }
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row--hop-ultra-repair .montibello-pdp-benefits__title {
    max-width: 470px;
    margin: 0 0 20px;
    font-size: 40px;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 40px;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    color: #000;

    @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
      max-width: none;
      font-size: 35px;
      line-height: 35px;
    }
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row--hop-ultra-repair .montibello-pdp-benefits__description {
    opacity: 1;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 19.7px;
    color: #000;
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row--hop-ultra-repair .montibello-pdp-benefits__description p {
    margin: 0 0 20px;
    padding: 0 0 20px;
    border-bottom: 0.5px solid #767676;
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits__photo-row--hop-ultra-repair .montibello-pdp-benefits__description p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* UNDER — Carta de Color CTA, relocated INTO this row's copy block
     (final punctual fix — see the `show_shade_cta` doc comment above).
     Same solid-black button treatment as the former standalone
     montibello-shade-browser section, just placed here instead so it reads
     as part of the lifestyle block rather than a separate band.

     WIDTH FIX (final minimal pass): `.copy` is a flex column
     (`display: flex; flex-direction: column`) with the default
     `align-items: stretch` — that stretches ANY child's cross-axis size to
     fill the column's full width regardless of the child's OWN `display`
     value, so `display: inline-flex` alone did not stop the button from
     being stretched edge-to-edge (confirmed live: it spanned the entire
     text column, reading as a wide bar instead of a compact button).
     `align-self: flex-start` opts this one child out of that stretch so its
     width is driven only by its own content + padding, and `width:
     fit-content` is kept as a belt-and-suspenders in case `align-self` is
     ever overridden by a future rule. */
  .montibello-pdp-benefits__shade-cta {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    align-self: flex-start;
    width: fit-content;
    gap: 10px;
    margin-top: 20px;
    padding: 14px 24px;
    background-color: #111111;
    color: #ffffff;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-decoration: none;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    white-space: nowrap;
    transition: background-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits__shade-cta:hover {
    background-color: #000000;
  }

  .montibello-pdp-benefits__shade-cta-icon {
    display: inline-flex;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  /* SCROLL REVEAL (FINAL 20/20 pass, Part 14) — ROOT CAUSE FIX: an earlier
     version of this reimplemented scroll-reveal from scratch with its own
     class name and CSS, which conflicted with an ALREADY-EXISTING,
     already-shared `[data-montibello-reveal]` convention used by
     sections/montibello-feature-rows.liquid, montibello-image-banner.liquid
     and montibello-stats-panel.liquid (JS: assets/montibello-scroll-
     reveal.js). Because Shopify bundles every section TYPE's own
     stylesheet-tag output theme-wide (not just on pages that render that
     section), those other sections' unconditional `[data-montibello-
     reveal] { opacity: 0; ... }` rule was ALSO present on this product
     page and — being declared after this file's rules in the bundle — won
     the cascade, while this file's own JS never added the `.is-visible`
     class that rule actually waits for. Net effect, confirmed live via a
     full-page screenshot: both Control Oil editorial sections rendered as
     permanently blank whitespace.

     Fixed by ADOPTING the existing shared convention exactly instead of
     inventing a second one: same attribute, same `.is-visible` reveal
     class, same values, and the same shared script include — see the
     `<script>` tag below, identical to how the other 3 sections use it. No
     new CSS/JS needed here at all. */
{% endstylesheet %}

<script src="{{ 'montibello-scroll-reveal.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "PDP Beneficios",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section-wrapper",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Título",
      "default": "Beneficios"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "shade_chart_url",
      "label": "URL del PDF (Carta de Color, solo UNDER Permanent Colour)",
      "info": "Reutiliza el mismo asset ya aprobado — no subir un PDF nuevo. Solo se muestra en el producto con datos de tonos (Permanent Colour); los activadores lo ignoran automáticamente."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "shade_chart_label",
      "label": "Texto del botón Carta de Color",
      "default": "Carta de Color"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "section_width",
      "label": "Ancho de sección",
      "options": [
        { "value": "page-width", "label": "Ancho de página" },
        { "value": "full-width", "label": "Ancho completo" }
      ],
      "default": "page-width"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-start",
      "label": "Superior",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 48
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-end",
      "label": "Inferior",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 48
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
